    "Description": "P1b (Hill-attack -> Blueprints migration): Action_CalculateSegments rebuilt as a visually-authored AiPrimitive BTreeAction, exercising GetParameter reads, a pure curated FunctionCall, and a straight-line SetVariable/Literal init chain against nine WorkingState fields. Graph: EventEntry -> SetVariable(TotalSlots) [Value wired from a pure FunctionCall Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.SegmentMath.TotalSlots(startX,startY,endX,endY,rawSpacing), whose five In pins are fed by five GetParameter reads (StartX,StartY,EndX,EndY,TankSpacing)] -> SetVariable(BurnedSlotsMask) <- Literal(System.UInt16 0) -> SetVariable(WaveUsedSlotsMask) <- Literal(System.UInt16 0) -> SetVariable(BaselineReservedMask) <- Literal(System.UInt16 0) -> SetVariable(ActiveAttackerCount) <- Literal(System.Int32 0) -> SetVariable(CurrentWave) <- Literal(System.Byte 0) -> SetVariable(CachedEqsRequestId) <- Literal(System.Int64 -1) -> SetVariable(CachedTargetGroupHandle) <- Literal(System.Int32 -1) -> SetVariable(EqsRequestTime) <- Literal(System.Single 0f) -> Return(Success). New curated helper: Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.SegmentMath.TotalSlots -- bundles the distance/clamp/spacing-default math (Vector2.Distance, the TankSpacing>0 ? TankSpacing : 30 default, Math.Max(1,...) then clamp to 16) that has no visual-node expression (architect Q#6-A: non-trivial math stays in reviewable curated helpers). Does not modify the C# oracle (HillAttackCommanderNodes.Action_CalculateSegments). Not reproduced: the oracle's BehaviorLog.IsDebugEnabled diagnostic logging call, which is a debug-only side channel with no bearing on WorkingState/return-status behavior.",
    "Category": null,
    "Recipe": null
